# Trivy CVE exception registry
#
# The primary suppression mechanism is --ignore-unfixed in ci.yml, which
# suppresses CVEs where no patched version exists yet (common for base image
# OS packages). Do not add entries here just because no fix exists — use
# --ignore-unfixed for that.
#
# Add an entry here ONLY when:
#   (a) A fix IS available but we cannot upgrade yet (blocking reason below), OR
#   (b) The CVE is a confirmed false positive (trivy misidentifies the component).
#
# Format: CVE-ID on its own line, mandatory comment with reason + expected resolution.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2099-12345  # python:3.12-slim openssl — fix in 3.12.11, blocked by
#                   # python-jose incompatibility; resolve by 2099-06-01
